  "id": "DrugBank_DB12141 - MONDO_18433",
  "verbalization": "Gilteritinib is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(6;9)(p23;q34) through a shared indication with Idarubicin, which in turn is linked to this leukemia subtype. This suggests a potential mechanism where Gilteritinib may exert its therapeutic effect on this leukemia type through a pathway involving Idarubicin. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Gilteritinib is implicated in the treatment of a subset of Acute Myeloid Leukemia cases, which share a common pathway with Idarubicin. The presence of a shared indication with Idarubicin, which is itself linked to Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(6;9)(p23;q34), implies that Gilteritinib may act through a mechanism that is complementary or overlapping with that of Idarubicin. The integration of these paths highlights a possible role for Gilteritinib in the treatment of this leukemia subtype, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
